>>regeneration  : food becomes a problem
Only use when necessary; food is rarely a problem.

>>conflict : great ring but use only when needed because you get no exper.
>points.    

>>levitation  : useless IMHO 
Of great use. People have been commenting lately on dieing in the moat
or other places by drowning. Solution: travel around the castle with a
ring of levetation on. DON'T take it off except to eat or pick up
goodies. Not only does this make it impossible to die of drowning
(thieveing nymphs notwithstanding), but you don't have to worry about
falling down any trapdoors. You don't waste a wish on boots of water
walking and you can keep your speed boots on. Also handy in hell if
you get sick of bear traps, or falling through trapdoors or into pits.
Wear it as you approach the altars in the endgame to ensure you avoid
the ultimate in annoying deaths; falling in the water as you are about
to #offer the amulet.
In short, after choking, falling in moats/pools is probably the most
common stupid death, and the ring of levetation is the best way to
avoid it.

